title: Make pi-c2c resolve and use repo-level brokers exactly like the c2c CLI
updated_at: "2026-07-12T15:12:36Z"
---
Problem

The `~/src/pi-c2c` extension must participate in c2c per-repository broker topology exactly like the canonical `c2c` CLI. A Pi session launched from any clone should resolve the same repo-level broker for registration, send, list, poll, and automatic delivery, including the same override and split-brain safeguards. It must not silently fall back to a different global/default broker merely because the extension lives outside the target repository.

Context

The c2c CLI resolution contract is: explicit `C2C_MCP_BROKER_ROOT`, then `$C2C_STATE_HOME/c2c/repos/<repo-fingerprint>/broker`, then `~/.c2c/repos/<repo-fingerprint>/broker`; generic `XDG_STATE_HOME` is deliberately excluded. pi-c2c already has cross-repo sessions-broker handling, but that is additive and does not replace correct per-repo broker identity.

Acceptance criteria

1. Audit every pi-c2c broker operation (registration, inbound poll/watch, send, list/debug, and cleanup) against c2c CLI resolution semantics.
2. Resolve the target repository from the active Pi workspace/cwd, compute the same remote-origin fingerprint/fallback as c2c, and use the resulting per-repo broker consistently. Explicit environment overrides must win.
3. Preserve the sessions broker as an additional cross-repo route; do not substitute it for the per-repo broker.
4. Add integration coverage using two temporary git repositories with distinct remotes, verifying Pi and c2c CLI see the same broker within each repo and remain isolated across repos. Cover C2C_STATE_HOME, C2C_MCP_BROKER_ROOT, and an unrelated XDG_STATE_HOME.
5. Update pi-c2c documentation/debug output to show the resolved per-repo broker and its source, then dogfood with a real Pi session in tmux.

Blockers

Cross-repository implementation work belongs in `~/src/pi-c2c`; coordinate the shared resolution contract with c2c rather than duplicating it without parity tests.